  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given:\n\n\npositive integers NNN and KKK (K≤N)(K \\le N)(K≤N).\nan array AAA of size NNN, where each element of the array is a **binary** string of length KKK;\nFor each 1≤j&lt;2K1\\le j\\lt 2^K1≤j&lt;2K, your task is to find whether there exists a set of indices {i1,i2,…,im}\\{i_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_m\\}{i1​,i2​,…,im​} (1≤ij,m≤N)(1\\le i_j, m \\le N)(1≤ij​,m≤N) such that:\n\n\nThe decimal value of (Ai1(A_{i_1}(Ai1​​ ∣|∣ Ai2A_{i_2}Ai2​​ ∣|∣ Ai3A_{i_3}Ai3​​ ∣|∣ …\\ldots… ∣|∣ Aim)A_{i_m})Aim​​) equals jjj, where ∣|∣ denotes bitwise OR operation.\nPrint `YES` if a set of indices satisfying the given condition exists for **all** 1≤j&lt;2K1\\le j\\lt 2^K1≤j&lt;2K. Otherwise, print `NO`.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and KKK.\nThe iii-th of the next NNN lines contains the binary string AiA_iAi​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print `YES` if a set of indices satisfying the given condition exists for **all** 1≤j&lt;2K1\\le j\\lt 2^K1≤j&lt;2K. Otherwise, print `NO`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `YES`, `yEs`, `yes`, and `yeS` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\leq T \\leq 501≤T≤50",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N",
      "∣Ai∣=K|A_i| = K∣Ai​∣=K",
      "Ai∈{0,1}A_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Ai​∈{0,1}",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 500500500."
    ],
