        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nj=1j = 1j=1 : The set of indices {1}\\{1\\}{1} satisfies the condition as decimal value of A1=1=jA_1 = 1 = jA1​=1=j.\nj=2j = 2j=2 : The set of indices {2}\\{2\\}{2} satisfies the condition as decimal value of A2=2=jA_2 = 2 = jA2​=2=j.\nj=3j = 3j=3 : The set of indices {1,2}\\{1, 2\\}{1,2} satisfies the condition as decimal value of (A1(A_1(A1​ ∣|∣ A2)=3=jA_2) = 3 = jA2​)=3=j.\n\nTest case 222: The set of indices for j=2,3,4,6,7j = 2, 3, 4, 6, 7j=2,3,4,6,7 are {2},{3},{4},{2,4},\\{2\\}, \\{3\\}, \\{4\\}, \\{2,4\\},{2},{3},{4},{2,4}, and {3,4}\\{3, 4\\}{3,4} respectively.\nHowever, there doesn't exist any set of indices for j=1j=1j=1 and j=5j=5j=5. Hence output is NO."
